```java
public static boolean isPowerOfThree(int n) {
    if (n <= 0) {
        return false;
    }
    int pow3 = 1;
    while (n > 0) {
        if (n % 3 == 0) {
            n /= 3;
        } else {
            pow3 *= 3;
        }
    }
    return pow3 == n;
}
```
The idea is to find the smallest power of 3 that is greater than or equal to the input `n`. We start with `pow3 = 1` and repeatedly divide `n` by 3 if it is divisible by 3, or multiply `pow3` by 3 if it is not. When `n` becomes 0, we return `pow3` since it must be a power of 3. If `n` is negative, we can simply return `false` since there is no x where 3^x = -n.

